1
00:00:00,833 --> 00:00:01,833
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,583 --> 00:00:08,208
When the name of Time
was still new,

3
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:09,375
there was a war

4
00:00:09,375 --> 00:00:12,250
in the First Realm of Creation,

5
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,708
a war between Dragons

6
00:00:14,708 --> 00:00:16,916
and their mortal enemies.

7
00:00:19,583 --> 00:00:22,291
A great warrior
of the Dragon army,

8
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:25,916
ThunderFang,
the Shatter Dragon of Chaos,

9
00:00:25,916 --> 00:00:27,875
believed his war victories

10
00:00:27,875 --> 00:00:31,833
entitled him to become
one of the Source Dragons.

11
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:34,458
When he was denied this honor,

12
00:00:34,458 --> 00:00:37,500
he unleashed chaos
upon the fabled...

13
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,833
City of Temples!

14
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:46,083
There, the devout followers
of the Source Dragons,

15
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:48,916
those who ran
the Tournament of Sources,

16
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:52,166
would've been destroyed
if it were not for...

17
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:57,458
...the Arc-Dragon of Focus!

18
00:00:57,458 --> 00:01:00,375
[roaring]

19
00:01:00,375 --> 00:01:03,958
[♪♪♪]

20
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:05,500
The Shatter Dragon,

21
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,750
whose powers were fueled

22
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:10,291
by the souls
of his consumed enemies,

23
00:01:10,291 --> 00:01:13,166
blasted weaponized storms
of chaotic power.

24
00:01:15,125 --> 00:01:19,666
Yet Focus is the natural enemy
of Chaos.

25
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,041
In victory,

26
00:01:24,041 --> 00:01:27,333
the Arc-Dragon of Focus
imprisoned ThunderFang

27
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:30,500
deep beneath the ground
of the First Realm,

28
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:35,208
where he remains, in chains,
to this day.

29
00:01:35,208 --> 00:01:37,333
But all
that has been chained

30
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:40,625
may one day be unchained.

31
00:01:40,625 --> 00:01:43,458
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

32
00:01:43,458 --> 00:01:45,750
♪ Together we will rise ♪

33
00:01:46,875 --> 00:01:50,375
♪ We fight ♪

34
00:01:50,375 --> 00:01:53,291
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪

35
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:05,208
[sighing]

36
00:02:05,208 --> 00:02:07,333
I bet Arin misses this place,
huh, Riyu?

37
00:02:13,041 --> 00:02:16,208
Sora, you're doing
Arin's old pie run?

38
00:02:16,208 --> 00:02:17,666
Lobbo lobbo!

39
00:02:17,666 --> 00:02:19,916
Yup, Arin's still missing,

40
00:02:19,916 --> 00:02:22,041
but us Ninja are working hard
on finding him.

41
00:02:23,291 --> 00:02:25,208
Until then, I thought I'd do
what Arin would do

42
00:02:25,208 --> 00:02:26,250
if he were still here...

43
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:27,541
baking pies

44
00:02:27,541 --> 00:02:30,666
and bringing them to all
Arin's friends and neighbors.

45
00:02:30,666 --> 00:02:32,708
Wonderful, thank you!

46
00:02:32,708 --> 00:02:34,583
Lobbo lobbo!

47
00:02:34,583 --> 00:02:35,916
[screaming]

48
00:02:35,916 --> 00:02:37,166
Distress!

49
00:02:37,166 --> 00:02:39,750
Total system shutdown!

50
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:41,416
Lobbo lobbo!

51
00:02:43,666 --> 00:02:44,958
I'm sure his reaction

52
00:02:44,958 --> 00:02:47,166
had nothing to do
with the quality of my pies.

53
00:02:50,208 --> 00:02:51,416
Free pie?

54
00:02:51,416 --> 00:02:52,666
Nothing better than--

55
00:02:53,958 --> 00:02:56,416
I need my stomach pumped
right now!

56
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:00,583
[spitting and screaming]

57
00:03:00,583 --> 00:03:01,583
[screaming]

58
00:03:03,416 --> 00:03:05,875
They can't be that bad.

59
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:07,333
Blech!

60
00:03:07,333 --> 00:03:10,750
[spewing and coughing]

61
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:12,916
I should probably seek
medical attention.

62
00:03:12,916 --> 00:03:14,125
Blech.

63
00:03:14,125 --> 00:03:15,208
I know what I need to do...

64
00:03:15,208 --> 00:03:17,250
but I don't like it.

65
00:03:19,291 --> 00:03:21,958
[♪♪♪]

66
00:03:32,833 --> 00:03:33,833
[popping noise]

67
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:34,833
Aah!

68
00:03:34,833 --> 00:03:35,833
Stop.

69
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:37,916
Stop what?

70
00:03:37,916 --> 00:03:40,250
That-- [groaning] --whatever!

71
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:41,541
That mouth noise.

72
00:03:41,541 --> 00:03:43,791
My mouth's not making
any noise, Nya.

73
00:03:43,791 --> 00:03:46,125
Well, it is now, but it wasn't.

74
00:03:47,458 --> 00:03:48,416
[lips popping]

75
00:03:48,416 --> 00:03:50,333
There! That's it.

76
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:51,333
You're doing it!

77
00:03:51,333 --> 00:03:52,333
[popping lips]

78
00:03:52,333 --> 00:03:53,625
Oh. [chuckling] Yeah.

79
00:03:53,625 --> 00:03:54,708
I didn't even realize.

80
00:03:54,708 --> 00:03:56,166
Bet that gets annoying.

81
00:03:56,166 --> 00:03:57,416
Yes!

82
00:03:57,416 --> 00:03:58,458
We gotta find Jay out here

83
00:03:58,458 --> 00:03:59,875
before
you drive me bonkers, Kai.

84
00:03:59,875 --> 00:04:01,333
Don't worry,

85
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:03,166
those reports
from the Explorer's Club

86
00:04:03,166 --> 00:04:04,333
about someone using lightning

87
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:05,583
came from right around here.

88
00:04:05,583 --> 00:04:06,875
It's gotta be Jay.

89
00:04:06,875 --> 00:04:09,166
He's the only lightning ninja
out there.

90
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:11,708
But he has no memory
of being a lightning ninja.

91
00:04:11,708 --> 00:04:13,083
I only hope when we find him,

92
00:04:13,083 --> 00:04:15,875
we can convince him
to come back with us.

93
00:04:15,875 --> 00:04:17,125
[popping lips]

94
00:04:17,125 --> 00:04:18,125
[screaming]

95
00:04:18,125 --> 00:04:19,000
Stop it!

96
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,958
Hey, you two! Hey!

97
00:04:20,958 --> 00:04:21,833
How can I stop it

98
00:04:21,833 --> 00:04:23,333
if I don't know I'm doing it?

99
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:25,083
I know a way to stop it!

100
00:04:25,083 --> 00:04:26,458
Hey!

101
00:04:26,458 --> 00:04:27,708
We found it.

102
00:04:27,708 --> 00:04:28,708
Look!

103
00:04:31,416 --> 00:04:34,250
Jay! It has to be him.

104
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:35,208
We can't just rush in.

105
00:04:35,208 --> 00:04:37,041
His goodness is shattered,
remember?

106
00:04:37,041 --> 00:04:39,416
Jay's more likely to fight us
than give us hugs.

107
00:04:39,416 --> 00:04:41,791
Wyldfyre, you flank
around the back and watch,

108
00:04:41,791 --> 00:04:43,833
in case we need backup.

109
00:04:45,375 --> 00:04:47,291
I'm just so worried about him.

110
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:48,875
Arin could be stuck
alone somewhere

111
00:04:48,875 --> 00:04:51,041
with Ras
and the Forbidden Five.

112
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:53,791
That's like a greatest hits
of evil warriors,

113
00:04:53,791 --> 00:04:56,333
and who even knows
where Jay could be?

114
00:04:56,333 --> 00:04:58,541
He's out there, alone,

115
00:04:58,541 --> 00:04:59,875
and without his memories.

116
00:04:59,875 --> 00:05:01,708
Nya, Kai, and Wyldfyre

117
00:05:01,708 --> 00:05:04,291
are following up on that lead
from the Explorer's Club.

118
00:05:04,291 --> 00:05:06,916
Zane is tracking
all the gate paths.

119
00:05:06,916 --> 00:05:09,000
We're doing
everything we can, Lloyd.

120
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,708
[sighing] I know,

121
00:05:10,708 --> 00:05:13,000
but I worry it's not enough.

122
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,833
And if they are truly lost,

123
00:05:14,833 --> 00:05:16,583
there's only one place
they'll end up.

124
00:05:16,583 --> 00:05:18,250
The Land of Lost Things?

125
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,625
Which is where I'm headed now.

126
00:05:20,625 --> 00:05:22,041
Me, Geo, and the Finders

127
00:05:22,041 --> 00:05:24,250
will search every inch
of that place.

128
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:26,166
Look...

129
00:05:26,166 --> 00:05:27,708
we're gonna find them,

130
00:05:27,708 --> 00:05:29,416
and bring us all back together.

131
00:05:29,416 --> 00:05:31,166
Like Master Wu said,

132
00:05:31,166 --> 00:05:32,791
"family is key."

133
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:37,208
I still can't believe
Master Wu caused the Merge.

134
00:05:37,208 --> 00:05:38,625
Why would he do that?

135
00:05:38,625 --> 00:05:39,750
I don't know,

136
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:42,041
but I heard it from
his semi-transparent lips

137
00:05:42,041 --> 00:05:43,250
myself.

138
00:05:43,250 --> 00:05:45,166
Do you really think
he's departed?

139
00:05:45,166 --> 00:05:47,250
Because it just doesn't...

140
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:49,166
feel like he's gone.

141
00:05:49,166 --> 00:05:50,375
With my history,

142
00:05:50,375 --> 00:05:52,791
I know what
departed spirits are.

143
00:05:52,791 --> 00:05:54,375
That was him.

144
00:05:54,375 --> 00:05:56,541
I'll send back anything I find.

145
00:05:57,625 --> 00:05:59,625
[sighing heavily]

146
00:06:07,083 --> 00:06:08,666
Haah!

147
00:06:08,666 --> 00:06:10,958
[breathing hard]

148
00:06:11,916 --> 00:06:12,958
Yaah!

149
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:15,791
[roaring]

150
00:06:18,208 --> 00:06:19,958
Oh, no, no, no!
Stop this!

151
00:06:19,958 --> 00:06:23,958
As Assistant Keeper
of this Monastery,

152
00:06:23,958 --> 00:06:25,833
I demand you halt!

153
00:06:25,833 --> 00:06:27,500
Do you know how hard it is

154
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:30,625
to find a proper
obstacle course repairman?

155
00:06:30,625 --> 00:06:32,750
Oh, uh...

156
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:35,083
Sorry, Mr. Frohicky.

157
00:06:39,666 --> 00:06:41,666
Did I-- do something wrong?

158
00:06:41,666 --> 00:06:43,416
That was a little...

159
00:06:43,416 --> 00:06:44,541
intense.

160
00:06:44,541 --> 00:06:45,791
Thank you, yes,

161
00:06:45,791 --> 00:06:47,750
I channeled all the strength
of my rage and hate.

162
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:50,666
You hate our obstacle course?

163
00:06:50,666 --> 00:06:52,000
No, I mean,

164
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,833
I channeled the hate inside me

165
00:06:53,833 --> 00:06:55,208
to access my potential.

166
00:06:55,208 --> 00:06:57,458
Isn't that how you do it?

167
00:06:57,458 --> 00:07:00,291
That's never been
the way of this monastery.

168
00:07:00,291 --> 00:07:02,000
Ras taught you that?

169
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,291
Yeah...

170
00:07:03,291 --> 00:07:05,500
Those kinds of emotions
give you strength.

171
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,750
I've seen it work.

172
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:08,916
There's more than one
source of strength,

173
00:07:08,916 --> 00:07:10,250
and physical strength alone

174
00:07:10,250 --> 00:07:12,125
isn't always
the best way to fight.

175
00:07:12,125 --> 00:07:14,416
I don't really understand,

176
00:07:14,416 --> 00:07:15,291
but that's okay.

177
00:07:15,291 --> 00:07:16,791
I'll stay up all night
practicing

178
00:07:16,791 --> 00:07:17,750
until I get it right!

179
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:20,000
I like that enthusiasm,

180
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,833
reminds me very much of Arin,

181
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:25,000
but maybe you should take
some time to rest.

182
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,833
"Rest"?

183
00:07:27,833 --> 00:07:29,208
Frak, uh...

184
00:07:29,208 --> 00:07:31,541
I know it's been awkward.

185
00:07:31,541 --> 00:07:34,375
You're Arin's old best friend,
I'm Arin's new best friend...

186
00:07:34,375 --> 00:07:36,250
I'm Arin's
always best friend.

187
00:07:37,333 --> 00:07:38,833
What I mean is,

188
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,041
with Arin gone,

189
00:07:40,041 --> 00:07:42,166
I'm trying to do
his pie run for him,

190
00:07:42,166 --> 00:07:46,166
but it turns out
I'm terrible at baking pies,

191
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:49,541
and since you're the one
who taught Arin to bake...

192
00:07:49,541 --> 00:07:50,708
Yes!

193
00:07:50,708 --> 00:07:52,333
The passing-on of pie knowledge!

194
00:07:52,333 --> 00:07:55,541
I have binders full of recipes!
I'll get everything ready!

195
00:07:57,291 --> 00:07:58,375
[groaning] Ugh...

196
00:07:58,375 --> 00:07:59,750
I regret this already.

197
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,333
[gasping] Jay!

198
00:08:03,333 --> 00:08:05,208
Jay, it's us!

199
00:08:07,041 --> 00:08:09,041
What? Who are you?

200
00:08:09,041 --> 00:08:10,291
How dare you disturb

201
00:08:10,291 --> 00:08:11,541
our once-in-a-decade

202
00:08:11,541 --> 00:08:14,916
sacred Lightning-Tide
Community Ceremony?

203
00:08:14,916 --> 00:08:17,583
[all groaning and shouting]

204
00:08:17,583 --> 00:08:19,791
Oh no, are you okay?

205
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:22,916
You ruined the whole ceremony!

206
00:08:22,916 --> 00:08:25,333
How dare you?

207
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:28,250
Attack the interlopers!

208
00:08:30,875 --> 00:08:33,208
Voilà! Perfect in every way!

209
00:08:33,208 --> 00:08:34,916
Now let's see yours, Sora!

210
00:08:37,208 --> 00:08:40,125
Uh, maybe it tastes... edible?

211
00:08:45,208 --> 00:08:46,041
[spitting]

212
00:08:46,041 --> 00:08:47,666
Ew, yeah.

213
00:08:47,666 --> 00:08:50,041
It has a very specific
rubber flavor

214
00:08:50,041 --> 00:08:52,125
not found in most pies.

215
00:08:52,125 --> 00:08:54,291
How can I be so bad at this?

216
00:08:54,291 --> 00:08:56,416
Look, everyone
starts out in a--

217
00:08:57,416 --> 00:08:59,166
Okay, that defies science.

218
00:08:59,166 --> 00:09:01,208
Let's start again from scratch.

219
00:09:03,041 --> 00:09:04,625
So, uh...

220
00:09:04,625 --> 00:09:07,250
do you have any opinions
on puppets?

221
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:09,208
Horrible, dead-eyed,
lifeless-limbed puppets?

222
00:09:09,208 --> 00:09:12,375
Wow, you're terrible
at small talk, aren't you?

223
00:09:12,375 --> 00:09:13,958
It's just that last night

224
00:09:13,958 --> 00:09:15,291
I saw this video of some guy

225
00:09:15,291 --> 00:09:16,750
describing a horrifying puppet

226
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:18,708
that's been attacking people
in the wastelands.

227
00:09:18,708 --> 00:09:20,041
This wouldn't be

228
00:09:20,041 --> 00:09:22,166
the "Intelligent George" show,
would it?

229
00:09:22,166 --> 00:09:24,791
You know it? They didn't
have that where I used to live.

230
00:09:24,791 --> 00:09:26,416
He's really full of wisdom.

231
00:09:27,791 --> 00:09:29,333
Don't believe
anything he says.

232
00:09:29,333 --> 00:09:31,833
Intelligent George
claims gravity is made up.

233
00:09:31,833 --> 00:09:33,000
Can you prove it's not?

234
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,291
I... have no idea
how to respond to that.

235
00:09:36,291 --> 00:09:38,083
I did once see
a weird robotic puppet

236
00:09:38,083 --> 00:09:39,166
in the Crossroads...

237
00:09:39,166 --> 00:09:41,750
Welp, never going
to the Crossroads again.

238
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,541
...but it's long gone,

239
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,000
so you have
nothing to fear, Frak.

240
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,166
Look, I know my pies
aren't the best,

241
00:09:47,166 --> 00:09:48,500
but Zane likes them.

242
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:49,541
You do?

243
00:09:49,541 --> 00:09:50,750
I find them adequate.

244
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:51,833
See?

245
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:54,125
Also, as a Nindroid,
I lack tastebuds.

246
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:55,750
[sighing]

247
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:57,291
Any progress on tracking Arin?

248
00:09:57,291 --> 00:09:59,083
Unfortunately not.

249
00:09:59,083 --> 00:10:01,208
I was hoping I could trace
the Gate system

250
00:10:01,208 --> 00:10:02,666
to determine where Arin, Ras,

251
00:10:02,666 --> 00:10:04,458
and the Forbidden Five
were transported,

252
00:10:04,458 --> 00:10:06,875
but so far, no luck.

253
00:10:06,875 --> 00:10:08,625
Nor have I had any
additional luck

254
00:10:08,625 --> 00:10:10,125
trying to find the smartest

255
00:10:10,125 --> 00:10:12,875
and most attractive
member of our team.

256
00:10:12,875 --> 00:10:14,375
But Sora's right here.

257
00:10:14,375 --> 00:10:16,291
-What?
-What? Uh... nothing.

258
00:10:16,291 --> 00:10:18,833
I was talking about P.I.X.A.L.

259
00:10:18,833 --> 00:10:20,458
[laughing awkwardly]
I knew that.

260
00:10:20,458 --> 00:10:21,875
[oven timer dinging]

261
00:10:21,875 --> 00:10:24,541
[sizzling and bubbling]

262
00:10:25,541 --> 00:10:26,541
[gasping]

263
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:34,083
[gasping] That is it!

264
00:10:35,208 --> 00:10:38,541
Maybe pie goo got in his gears
or something.

265
00:10:38,541 --> 00:10:40,291
[pie bubbling and exploding]

266
00:10:45,666 --> 00:10:49,250
Are you really watching
my "pie fail" on loop?

267
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:51,208
You don't think
I find this whole situation

268
00:10:51,208 --> 00:10:52,875
humiliating enough already?

269
00:10:52,875 --> 00:10:54,375
But it is genius.

270
00:10:54,375 --> 00:10:55,958
Comedic genius, I agree.

271
00:10:55,958 --> 00:10:57,625
It's not that funny.

272
00:10:57,625 --> 00:10:59,833
Although I did not mean
"comedic genius,"

273
00:10:59,833 --> 00:11:03,291
I do see how it definitely
could be interpreted as such.

274
00:11:03,291 --> 00:11:04,416
[Sora groaning]

275
00:11:04,416 --> 00:11:06,250
But the genius
I am referring to

276
00:11:06,250 --> 00:11:07,375
is the manner in which

277
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:09,375
it is helping me discover
what happened to Arin.

278
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:11,208
-You're joking.
-I am not.

279
00:11:11,208 --> 00:11:13,083
I had been tracking
the possible trajectories

280
00:11:13,083 --> 00:11:15,416
of Arin passing through
the exploding portal.

281
00:11:15,416 --> 00:11:17,750
I theorized the explosion
dumped the travelers

282
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,708
to a random place
in the Merged Lands,

283
00:11:19,708 --> 00:11:21,958
but when I tried
to model the equation,

284
00:11:21,958 --> 00:11:24,500
I obtained no tangible results,

285
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:27,208
but your chaotic
and comedic pie explosion

286
00:11:27,208 --> 00:11:29,958
made me realize
that space-folding gateways

287
00:11:29,958 --> 00:11:32,708
may operate
under chaotic variables...

288
00:11:32,708 --> 00:11:34,958
variables
I had not been accounting for.

289
00:11:34,958 --> 00:11:37,708
Once I incorporate
this new data...

290
00:11:37,708 --> 00:11:39,333
[keyboarding]

291
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:41,041
Yes, that is it!

292
00:11:41,041 --> 00:11:43,541
It's only a general idea
where Arin could have gone,

293
00:11:43,541 --> 00:11:45,875
but it's the best lead
we have so far.

294
00:11:45,875 --> 00:11:47,208
We need to find him.

295
00:11:47,208 --> 00:11:48,750
Baking pies can wait.

296
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:49,875
If you call that baking.

297
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:50,875
Please stop talking.

298
00:11:53,208 --> 00:11:55,083
Behold!

299
00:11:55,083 --> 00:11:57,916
Lightning-Tides of the Court,

300
00:11:57,916 --> 00:12:00,958
as I lay out indisputable proof

301
00:12:00,958 --> 00:12:03,625
that the completely guilty
strangers

302
00:12:03,625 --> 00:12:05,791
are guilty!

303
00:12:05,791 --> 00:12:08,125
First, they interrupted

304
00:12:08,125 --> 00:12:11,458
our much-beloved
sacred ceremony.

305
00:12:11,458 --> 00:12:12,916
Then,

306
00:12:12,916 --> 00:12:15,666
their stench
is rather pungent.

307
00:12:15,666 --> 00:12:17,375
The one in red also has a voice

308
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:20,000
that sounds like gargling slime.

309
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,083
Hey!

310
00:12:21,083 --> 00:12:23,958
See? Repulsive.

311
00:12:23,958 --> 00:12:25,625
[pounding]

312
00:12:25,625 --> 00:12:27,000
Gross.

313
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Does the defense have
any response

314
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,916
to this convincing evidence?

315
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:35,416
Listen, yes, my clients
are clearly guilty,

316
00:12:35,416 --> 00:12:38,083
but, um, uh...

317
00:12:38,083 --> 00:12:39,333
I got nothing.

318
00:12:39,333 --> 00:12:41,666
I thought something'd
come to me, but it didn't.

319
00:12:41,666 --> 00:12:43,166
You call that a defense?

320
00:12:43,166 --> 00:12:44,916
Uh, I'd now like to add

321
00:12:44,916 --> 00:12:47,041
"Speaking
In A Gargle Slime Voice

322
00:12:47,041 --> 00:12:48,208
With A Tinge Of Smugness"

323
00:12:48,208 --> 00:12:49,416
to the charges.

324
00:12:49,416 --> 00:12:51,583
The defense rests. [chuckling]

325
00:12:51,583 --> 00:12:53,208
If that is all,

326
00:12:53,208 --> 00:12:56,416
I would like
to pass a sentence of...

327
00:12:56,416 --> 00:12:59,291
The Punishment
of 1,003 Zappings!

328
00:12:59,291 --> 00:13:00,375
Hold it!

329
00:13:00,375 --> 00:13:01,291
[quietly] I got this.

330
00:13:01,291 --> 00:13:03,375
Look, this entire situation

331
00:13:03,375 --> 00:13:05,541
has just been
a misunderstanding.

332
00:13:05,541 --> 00:13:06,708
My brother here and I--

333
00:13:06,708 --> 00:13:07,708
Run!

334
00:13:07,708 --> 00:13:08,916
[cackling]

335
00:13:13,625 --> 00:13:15,958
Come on, Nya,
I've got you covered.

336
00:13:20,208 --> 00:13:21,208
Vengestone?

337
00:13:21,208 --> 00:13:22,958
It cancels elemental powers!

338
00:13:22,958 --> 00:13:24,541
Where did you get Vengestone?

339
00:13:24,541 --> 00:13:26,916
That was my favorite bench!

340
00:13:26,916 --> 00:13:30,000
You're going to get
double punished now!

341
00:13:31,208 --> 00:13:32,250
Ow!

342
00:13:32,250 --> 00:13:34,041
Why did you do that, Kai?

343
00:13:34,041 --> 00:13:36,375
I told you I had this!

344
00:13:36,375 --> 00:13:38,083
I thought you meant
you had a distraction

345
00:13:38,083 --> 00:13:38,958
so I could blast stuff!

346
00:13:38,958 --> 00:13:40,041
Why would I mean that?

347
00:13:40,041 --> 00:13:41,875
Cause that's what
I always hope people mean.

348
00:13:41,875 --> 00:13:42,750
[lock clanking]

349
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:52,916
This is the general area
indicated by my calculations.

350
00:13:52,916 --> 00:13:55,875
I don't see any sign
of Arin, Ras, or the others.

351
00:13:58,666 --> 00:14:00,250
Let's check with
whoever lives here.

352
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:02,083
Maybe they saw something.

353
00:14:02,083 --> 00:14:03,916
[sniffing]

354
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:07,083
[knocking]

355
00:14:07,083 --> 00:14:08,750
Excuse me,

356
00:14:08,750 --> 00:14:10,000
sorry to bother you,

357
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,875
but we're looking
for my best friend--

358
00:14:11,875 --> 00:14:13,041
Go away!

359
00:14:13,041 --> 00:14:15,250
You'll bring
its creepy wrath upon us all!

360
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:16,291
[slamming door]

361
00:14:16,291 --> 00:14:18,625
Okay, trying not
to take that personally.

362
00:14:19,791 --> 00:14:22,000
What's the "it"
they're talking about?

363
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
That can bring
a creepy wrath?

364
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,291
Don't like those words.

365
00:14:25,291 --> 00:14:27,833
[roaring]

366
00:14:30,541 --> 00:14:31,958
[roaring]

367
00:14:33,916 --> 00:14:35,375
[roaring]

368
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:38,083
Intelligent George was right.

369
00:14:38,083 --> 00:14:39,458
[roaring]

370
00:14:45,125 --> 00:14:47,708
Come on,
it's Dorama's old puppet!

371
00:14:47,708 --> 00:14:49,458
We've stopped
this thing before!

372
00:14:49,458 --> 00:14:51,791
Those lifeless, dead eyes...

373
00:14:51,791 --> 00:14:53,625
[snarling]

374
00:14:56,833 --> 00:14:59,000
[Sora] The eye-lasers
are new, right?

375
00:15:00,125 --> 00:15:02,666
Yeah, and deadly!

376
00:15:03,916 --> 00:15:05,708
Hey, where did you get
the Vengestone?

377
00:15:05,708 --> 00:15:07,500
You mean the Glow Rocks?

378
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,333
Dunno, we found them.

379
00:15:09,333 --> 00:15:11,583
Thought they'd be fun
to throw at you.

380
00:15:11,583 --> 00:15:13,250
So you didn't know

381
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:15,041
they stopped
elemental powers?

382
00:15:15,041 --> 00:15:17,041
Uh, stopped what, now?

383
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:18,208
Order! Order!

384
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:20,791
We now must double punish
our captives,

385
00:15:20,791 --> 00:15:24,666
as soon as we determine
how many "double" is.

386
00:15:24,666 --> 00:15:27,208
[Wyldfyre]
No need for such silly ideas!

387
00:15:32,166 --> 00:15:35,166
I, as you can see,
am a Lava-Tide...

388
00:15:35,166 --> 00:15:36,416
[groaning]

389
00:15:36,416 --> 00:15:37,583
[winking]

390
00:15:37,583 --> 00:15:41,000
...and I have just received
this very official pardon

391
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,416
from the, uh...

392
00:15:42,416 --> 00:15:44,375
uh, Lava-Tide President,

393
00:15:44,375 --> 00:15:46,416
demanding all charges
against these Ninjas--

394
00:15:46,416 --> 00:15:47,833
Hurl the glow rocks!

395
00:15:47,833 --> 00:15:49,708
Ah! Ugh!

396
00:15:55,375 --> 00:15:56,375
[roaring]

397
00:15:57,416 --> 00:15:59,791
Okay, that thing lasers.

398
00:15:59,791 --> 00:16:01,833
I don't see Dorama anywhere.

399
00:16:01,833 --> 00:16:03,916
Did his puppet escape from him?

400
00:16:03,916 --> 00:16:05,833
Here, let me make
quick work of it.

401
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:20,458
Okay, so it's not running
on any sort of technology now.

402
00:16:20,458 --> 00:16:21,333
Magic?

403
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:24,250
This is not happening.

404
00:16:25,458 --> 00:16:26,791
[panting in terror]

405
00:16:28,083 --> 00:16:30,250
[roaring]

406
00:16:33,083 --> 00:16:35,333
Intelligent George
was right about this puppet!

407
00:16:35,333 --> 00:16:37,500
I think this also proves
that gravity isn't real.

408
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:40,083
I'm not going to engage
in this conversation.

409
00:16:44,666 --> 00:16:45,541
[roaring]

410
00:16:45,541 --> 00:16:46,708
[grunting]

411
00:16:55,375 --> 00:16:56,250
[Frak] That glow...

412
00:16:56,250 --> 00:16:57,208
[roaring]

413
00:16:58,625 --> 00:17:01,291
Maybe this is what you were
teaching me earlier, Lloyd?

414
00:17:01,291 --> 00:17:02,625
I don't remember
teaching anything

415
00:17:02,625 --> 00:17:05,125
about bizarre puppet fighting.

416
00:17:05,125 --> 00:17:06,125
[roaring]

417
00:17:07,625 --> 00:17:09,875
No, I mean, maybe
physical strength alone

418
00:17:09,875 --> 00:17:11,458
isn't the best way
to win this fight?

419
00:17:13,625 --> 00:17:14,625
Oh, no.

420
00:17:14,625 --> 00:17:15,750
I know what I need to do,

421
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:17,416
but I don't like it.

422
00:17:19,250 --> 00:17:20,791
[wailing in terror]

423
00:17:20,791 --> 00:17:22,791
[roaring]

424
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:25,458
Aah! Why do puppets
move all creepy?

425
00:17:25,458 --> 00:17:28,416
We gotta help him!
Keep it distracted!

426
00:17:31,375 --> 00:17:32,458
[grunting with effort] H'yah!

427
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:34,625
Frak, what are you doing?

428
00:17:34,625 --> 00:17:36,083
[Frak] Facing my primal fears!

429
00:17:36,083 --> 00:17:37,291
What does it look
like I'm doing?

430
00:17:37,291 --> 00:17:40,000
Yeah, but what are you doing
that can help us?

431
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,625
I saw a glow from outside!

432
00:17:41,625 --> 00:17:44,625
Maybe something's powering
this walking nightmare.

433
00:17:44,625 --> 00:17:46,333
[straining]

434
00:17:47,833 --> 00:17:49,375
[roaring]

435
00:17:58,166 --> 00:17:59,583
[yelping, slamming heavily]

436
00:18:00,875 --> 00:18:01,875
Is it over?

437
00:18:01,875 --> 00:18:03,500
I'm stuck! I'm stuck!

438
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:04,583
[sobbing in terror]

439
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:06,333
Get me out of this thing!

440
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:09,208
What happened to
facing your primal fears?

441
00:18:09,208 --> 00:18:10,208
Ah!

442
00:18:10,208 --> 00:18:11,916
I faced them, and lost.

443
00:18:11,916 --> 00:18:13,875
I'm now a million times
more afraid of puppets.

444
00:18:15,916 --> 00:18:17,500
Thank you!

445
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:19,958
The puppet's fearful reign
has finally ended.

446
00:18:19,958 --> 00:18:23,083
Huzzah!

447
00:18:23,083 --> 00:18:26,375
I do not know exactly how
this empowered the marionette,

448
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:28,708
but it is an item
of immense energy.

449
00:18:28,708 --> 00:18:30,541
Then we should keep it.

450
00:18:30,541 --> 00:18:32,208
Too dangerous
to leave sitting out here.

451
00:18:32,208 --> 00:18:34,166
[Sora] And it looks like
we're on the right track.

452
00:18:34,166 --> 00:18:35,916
That sword
wasn't the only thing

453
00:18:35,916 --> 00:18:37,333
caught in this puppet.

454
00:18:37,333 --> 00:18:38,583
Arin's grapple!

455
00:18:41,208 --> 00:18:43,166
Hey, look, are these tracks?

456
00:18:43,166 --> 00:18:45,875
[Riyu sniffing]

457
00:18:46,666 --> 00:18:47,750
[roaring]

458
00:18:54,916 --> 00:18:58,166
3,000 zaps is more
than 2,000 zaps, right?

459
00:18:58,166 --> 00:18:59,708
Oh, maybe?

460
00:18:59,708 --> 00:19:01,333
[gasping] Counterpoint.

461
00:19:01,333 --> 00:19:03,083
Maybe not?

462
00:19:03,083 --> 00:19:06,625
As a judge,
my wisdom is extraordinary.

463
00:19:06,625 --> 00:19:09,083
They are equal.

464
00:19:09,083 --> 00:19:11,500
Look, let me try this again,

465
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:12,833
without my annoying brother

466
00:19:12,833 --> 00:19:14,666
and his clueless friend
messing it all up.

467
00:19:14,666 --> 00:19:17,083
Who's your clueless friend?

468
00:19:17,083 --> 00:19:18,416
This entire situation

469
00:19:18,416 --> 00:19:20,708
has just been
a misunderstanding.

470
00:19:20,708 --> 00:19:23,583
We came here to find
a missing person.

471
00:19:23,583 --> 00:19:25,625
His name is Jay Walker,

472
00:19:25,625 --> 00:19:27,875
and I love him very much.

473
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:29,041
We all do.

474
00:19:29,041 --> 00:19:30,791
I haven't met him,
to be honest.

475
00:19:30,791 --> 00:19:33,166
Jay is funny, charming,

476
00:19:33,166 --> 00:19:35,208
cute, sincere,

477
00:19:35,208 --> 00:19:37,416
the real heart
of our Ninja team.

478
00:19:37,416 --> 00:19:38,583
Not sure that's accurate.

479
00:19:38,583 --> 00:19:39,916
We interrupted your ceremony

480
00:19:39,916 --> 00:19:41,958
not out of spite or cruelty,

481
00:19:41,958 --> 00:19:44,291
just out of innocent confusion.

482
00:19:44,291 --> 00:19:45,833
Jay has lightning powers,

483
00:19:45,833 --> 00:19:46,916
and we thought,

484
00:19:46,916 --> 00:19:48,083
we hoped,

485
00:19:48,083 --> 00:19:50,916
we were about to find
our long-lost friend.

486
00:19:51,958 --> 00:19:54,458
[sniffling and crying]

487
00:19:54,458 --> 00:19:55,958
[clapping]

488
00:19:55,958 --> 00:19:57,375
Well said.

489
00:19:57,375 --> 00:20:00,125
If there's one thing
us Tide-folk understand,

490
00:20:00,125 --> 00:20:02,250
it's innocent confusion.

491
00:20:02,250 --> 00:20:03,500
You are free to go.

492
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:04,500
[removing lock]

493
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:10,416
Excuse me,

494
00:20:10,416 --> 00:20:13,250
but she explained
her case very well.

495
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:14,541
You two, on the other hand,

496
00:20:14,541 --> 00:20:15,958
are going nowhere.

497
00:20:15,958 --> 00:20:17,083
What? Ha!

498
00:20:17,083 --> 00:20:19,083
You think my sister
would just leave us here?

499
00:20:20,375 --> 00:20:22,458
Nya?

500
00:20:22,458 --> 00:20:23,916
[sighing]

501
00:20:26,625 --> 00:20:29,791
Guess there really is
only one way out of this place.

502
00:20:38,666 --> 00:20:39,666
[winking]

503
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:42,250
[Kai] I knew
you'd never abandon me!

504
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:43,541
[Nya] Don't make me regret it!

505
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:01,541
We need those supplies.

506
00:21:01,541 --> 00:21:02,416
Zarkt?

507
00:21:10,083 --> 00:21:12,333
[yelping in fright]

508
00:21:12,333 --> 00:21:13,458
[groaning]

509
00:21:14,458 --> 00:21:16,291
Well done, Kur,

510
00:21:16,291 --> 00:21:17,458
but let them live.

511
00:21:17,458 --> 00:21:20,000
Now they will warn others

512
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,625
that the Forbidden Five
have returned...

513
00:21:22,625 --> 00:21:25,208
[furious buzzing of insects]

514
00:21:25,208 --> 00:21:27,791
...and no one is safe!

515
00:21:27,791 --> 00:21:30,875
[laughing maniacally]

516
00:21:30,875 --> 00:21:33,291
Pillage
whatever supplies we need

517
00:21:33,291 --> 00:21:36,166
for our journey
to the First Land.

518
00:21:36,166 --> 00:21:40,416
It's time to unchain
ThunderFang!

519
00:21:44,958 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

